{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/231671-titans-the-conquerors","id":231671,"title":"Titans, the conquerors!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-17T10:42:28-07:00","id":231671,"title":"Titans, the conquerors!","content":"I still don't really understand how Titans could win over Gods... Everything that exist is because of the Titans. Earth, Sky, Chaos, Sun. If Titans kill the Gods and destroy the universe (I'm sure that Earth is not the only place they are going to destroy), how would they keep on existing and why would they? What good would that bring them to do that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T12:57:40-07:00","id":231882,"title":"","content":"That's kind of the point. Right now, the Titans have just woken up. They are lashing out blindly. That is why the gods have the upper hand. That is why they think they can win this war. Also, the Titans are just mindless attacking anything. They do not WANT to destroy the universe...but they will if they keep this up. So the gods have activated their children to go out and stop the Titans before they wake up fully and organize and also before they do crash the cosmos with their insanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T14:05:27-07:00","id":231941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/231671-titans-the-conquerors?p=231882#post231882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's kind of the point. Right now, the Titans have just woken up. They are lashing out blindly. That is why the gods have the upper hand. That is why they think they can win this war. Also, the Titans are just mindless attacking anything. They do not WANT to destroy the universe...but they will if they keep this up. So the gods have activated their children to go out and stop the Titans before they wake up fully and organize and also before they do crash the cosmos with their insanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, it bears mentioning that even without destroying the universe or somesuch the Titans are quite capable of turning the Earth on something unhabitable for most lifeforms or at least a hell on earth, for the sake of convenience and personal preferences as rapacious personified elemental forces that they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T15:21:59-07:00","id":232014,"title":"","content":"So no goal for now because still warming up but if they come to act smart, they might wanna make the Earth a unhabitable place?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T15:36:12-07:00","id":232024,"title":"","content":"Well, the key to remember is that it would be uninhabitable for <i>us</i>. If the titan of fire turns earth into a volcanic wasteland, we would be dead but the fire giants would be just peachy. <br /> <br /> Also, the titans aren't dependent on humanity for their existence, but instead their element. So for them, turning the earth into a fireball/realm of eternal darkness/etc. would only empower them more. Sure, after they beat the gods they will have to beat their own allies to establish their world view, but that is a post war concern for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T23:03:13-07:00","id":232476,"title":"","content":"That was my next question. It's easier to see it that way, that Titans and Gods were created before humanity. But if Titans and Gods were created by humanity's stories as suggested in the book? They would have come after and if mortals' stories guide every myth, it could change the whole thing! But it's getting too complicated and I'm not sure I want any suggestion about this haha... I thought it could be interesting but... headache!<br /> <br /> One more question. Why beating the Gods is okay? Titans should not be kill because they embody what they are. That's very true for the Gods, too. Who will embody justice if every God of justice gets killed? The Titans only embody the raw elements... is that enough or the concept would disappear with the dead God?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T04:04:55-07:00","id":232653,"title":"","content":"The Titans don't care if Justice goes away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/370-oriares","name":"Oriares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar370_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T05:14:19-07:00","id":232705,"title":"","content":"The gods never cared about justice until recently.<br /> Not all titans were bad. Some were friends to man.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T09:39:42-07:00","id":232911,"title":"","content":"There is one conceptual Titan mentioned in the books, Logos, who would probably count as a Titan of Justice, with examples of Avatars like Ma'at and Metis. Justice (like Fate?) is out there as an absolute. Like Fire, Light, Darkness, etc. <br /> <br /> So, at least ONE Titan cares if Justice goes away. Maybe not the gods of justice, but the fundamental concept. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T09:48:32-07:00","id":232917,"title":"","content":"Define &quot;justice&quot; as it was over 5000 years ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T15:43:25-07:00","id":233348,"title":"","content":"The Gods and Titans came before man, but the Gods chose to shelter and interact with humanity, leading to their fates becoming tied to the stories told by man, and also freeing them from control by the titans (remember, they are titanspawn... technically). Think of it as actors becoming typecast. The actor existed before the movies they were in, but each time they were cast in a similar role, the more they became known as &quot;that guy&quot;. The Titans remained true to the Elements they govern, and thus were not dependent on man nor fate bound aignificantly. <br /> <br /> Yes, some titans were &quot;beneficial&quot; but only towards their own ends. Promethazine gave us technology without the wisdom of its use, so as to strengthen his own domain. He doesn't care if we use nukes to wipeout all of humanity, just that they are developed and used. <br /> <br /> Logos is the only beneficial Titan, and mostly because Logos was neutral. The concept of Justice as an eternal force though, pre human culture, is a bit odd. Though thus may reflect the concept of eternal abstracts (I.e. that truth always exists, even if no one ever has told a lie, as truth represents an expression and recognition of the actual nature of something).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T16:20:57-07:00","id":233381,"title":"","content":"The gods chose to shelter humanity? I don't think so. O...yeah, as Scion goes, that may be the case now, but in the beginning? Not so. the concept of justice varied from culture to culture. And primarily (as posted before) was meant to maintain the rule of Law (order) This order supported slavery in most cultures, caste systems, and held a strong prejudice against other city states. (ancient Lex Talionis, sometimes referred to as &quot;eye for an eye...Maat with various taboos that look in some spots like the Ten Commandments, which is yet another)....And regarding certain titans, it's not a good idea to adhere to Scion 1E as for example, <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prometheus\" target=\"_blank\">Prometheus</a> was awesome; <i>Prometheus tricks Zeus into eternally claiming the inedible parts of cows and bulls for the sacrificial ceremonies of the Gods, while conceding the nourishing parts to humans for the eternal benefit of humankind. The two remaining central episodes regarding Prometheus as written by Hesiod include his theft of fire from Olympus for the benefit of humanity against the will of Zeus, and the eternal punishment which Prometheus would endure for these acts as inflicted upon him by the judgment of Zeus.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T19:58:36-07:00","id":233658,"title":"","content":"Obviously I wasn't using the actual mythos, but the setting itself. The fact that many of the &quot;titans&quot; weren't progenitors but just gods associated with not bowing to the established Pantheons is obvious. I am only working within the games mythology to construct the theories, not those of the actual myths. That would be like arguing that Werewolf the Frosaken/Apocalypse are idiots for using Silver as the werewolves weakness as te in game mythology says it is a curse associated with the spirit Luna (rather than the general mythology that silver is a pure and sacred metal that works on nearly every evil undead thing... and it not becoming the werewolves specific weakness wasn't till the 20th century). Yes, in our mythology, Prometheus was actually a good guy. The game even acknowledges that, before giving &quot;the true story&quot; as per what the game mythology calls for. Considering that the OP is asking about the Titans and God's in the setting of the game, going beyond that to argue the nature of the source mythology is just misleading the topic. So, for the sake of this Topic, per the Scion mythos, the Titans are all right bastards and the Gods were humanities abusive protectors (I am not saying they were good guardians, just that they kept the titans from killing us).<br /> <br /> As for the issue of Law and Justice, that is why I referred to the abstract of Justice, not its mundane form. The abstract would reflect the concept of identifying, fairly trying and rewarding/punishing actions. And most cultures quickly developed thesee rudimentary concepts, even if they chose to then ignore them at occasions or apply them only to specific individuals. Hence Logos being the Titan, remaining removed from humanities ideas and focusing on the Ideal of Justice, not the cultural (and as you pointed out, the gods can be jerks. Many abuses of Justice were justified as religiously necessary, from defied kings/kings who ruled by divine right, to human sacrafice, even in this games setting).<br /> <br /> Finally, per the Titans, Justice is a counter to Chaos (the titan of chaos has less resistance to harm from justice based boons), indicating it might also reflect the primordial force of Order, with Justice being how it manifests within humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","user":"Freemind","date":". 08-18-2014, 11:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T22:51:59-07:00","id":272760,"title":"","content":"Well if you're going to say the Titans were monstrous bastards, I think that's a matter of perspective. It sounds like the Titans were the personifications of nature and reality itself. In regards to humans personally, yes, they would have been evil. But on the grand scope of the universe? They're just doing what is within their nature to do. The universe does not bow to the whims of humanity, however much it might wish it to do so.<br /> <br /> A Titan of power and chaos is utterly incapable of learning or even comprehending the desire to save the weak, or follow a strict set of rules. It is chaos incarnate, and Chaos says screw the rules!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}